    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nI would like to add support for user-defined highlighting inside `mini.files`. This would allow for users to define something like:\n\n```lua\nrequire(\"mini.files\").setup({\n  content = {\n    highlight = function(fs_entry)\n      if fs_entry.fs_type == 'file' then\n        if vim.startswith(fs_entry.name, '.') then\n          return 'MiniFilesHidden'\n        end\n      end\n      return nil\n    end,\n  }\n})\n\n```\n\nResulting in:\n\n<img width=\"830\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/277e58fd-1554-46ca-884c-14fec7282e3c\" />\n\nHere is a [draft implementation](https://github.com/kennykaye/mini.files/commit/02af945b7fadcc447d1628f4afbf5fa32b4ea5a2). If this is something you would be interested in, I could move this against the main project.\n\nAlternatives considered:\n* Adding hardcoded support for a `MiniFilesHidden` highlight group",
